<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Retro on 0x32++</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/retro/</link><description>Recent content in Retro on 0x32++</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/tags/retro/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Doomheaven Moves to GitHub Pages</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/doomheaven-github-pages/</link><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/doomheaven-github-pages/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://doomheaven.uk"&gt;doomheaven.uk&lt;/a&gt; is moving house.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;It started life as a Doom fan site back in the late 90s — WADs, screenshots, whatever bits of Doom nonsense felt worth putting on the web at the time. It&amp;rsquo;s sat online quietly ever since, hosted the whole way through by &lt;a href="https://teamhellspawn.com"&gt;teamhellspawn.com&lt;/a&gt;, who&amp;rsquo;ve now let me know they&amp;rsquo;re winding things down.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;I want to say a proper thank you to them for that. Free webspace for the better part of three decades is a genuinely long time to keep something ticking over for no reason beyond being decent about it, and rather than just switching it off, they gave me the chance to get everything off in one piece before it went. Not everyone bothers with that on the way out, so it was appreciated.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>BBC Twitter Bot Fun</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/bbcbot/</link><pubDate>Wed, 19 Jan 2022 13:48:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/bbcbot/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;More fun playing with BBC Twitter Bot.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;https://tco/ks0jhudxdM&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://t.co/xBabCMPWCX"&gt;https://t.co/xBabCMPWCX&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;https://tco/jVpUMLBa8D&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;https://tco/Rt3DOf1FOh&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Beebasm Mac Catalina</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/beebasm/</link><pubDate>Thu, 14 Jan 2021 16:50:36 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/beebasm/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Got a new Mac with Catalina pre-installed, so had to compile my own version of &lt;a href=""&gt;Beebasm&lt;/a&gt; for the 64 bit OS.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://blog.0x32.co.uk/beebasm.zip"&gt;BeebAsm.zip&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>10 PRINT6502</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10print6502/</link><pubDate>Fri, 11 Dec 2020 15:15:26 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10print6502/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;BBC Micro machine code take on &lt;a href="https://10print.org/"&gt;C64 10 Print&lt;/a&gt; one line random pattern generator.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Code at Github &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/beebasm/blob/master/examples/10print.asm"&gt;10print.asm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;figure class="wp-caption alignnone"&gt;&#10; &lt;a data-flickr-embed="true" data-header="true" data-footer="false"&#10; data-context="false"&#10; href="https://www.flickr.com/photos/doodle_m/50706346667"&#10; title="10 PRINT 6502"&gt;&#10; &lt;img src="https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/50706346667_1e2bf3b7a9_c.jpg" width="800" alt="10 PRINT 6502" /&gt;&#10; &lt;/a&gt;&lt;script async src="//embedr.flickr.com/assets/client-code.js" charset="utf-8"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;&#10; &lt;figcaption class="wp-caption-text"&gt;10 PRINT 6502&lt;/figcaption&gt;&#10; &lt;/figure&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;div class="code-block"&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="code-copy" type="button" hidden aria-label="Copy code to clipboard"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="code-copy-label" aria-hidden="true"&gt;Copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-asm" data-lang="asm"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;10&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;PRINT&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;Using&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;BeebASM&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;assembler&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;\&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;(&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;c&lt;/span&gt;) &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;Alastair&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;Montgomery&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;INCLUDE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;..&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;lib&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;constants.asm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;70&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;ORG&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;amp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;2000&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.start&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;LDA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#23&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;STA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;LDA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#63&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;STA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;seed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;+&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;1&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;LDX&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#0&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.char&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;LDA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;chartable&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;X&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;JSR&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;oswrch&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;INX&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;CPX&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#23&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;BNE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;char&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.loop&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;JSR&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;random&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;BMI&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;two&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.one&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;LDA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#224&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;JMP&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;print&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.two&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;LDA&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#75715e"&gt;#225&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.print&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;JSR&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;oswrch&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;JMP&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;loop&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.finish&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;RTS&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.random&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;INCLUDE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;..&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;lib&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;random.asm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.chartable&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;EQUB&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;22&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;EQUB&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;23&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;224&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;224&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;48&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;16&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;16&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;EQUB&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;23&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;225&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;16&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;16&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;48&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;224&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;7&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;12&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;,&lt;span style="color:#ae81ff"&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;.end&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#a6e22e"&gt;SAVE&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;MyCode&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="color:#960050;background-color:#1e0010"&gt;&amp;#34;&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;start&lt;/span&gt;, &lt;span style="color:#66d9ef"&gt;end&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>6502 Assembly Language</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/6502/</link><pubDate>Thu, 26 Nov 2020 16:54:08 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/6502/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Been trying to relearn 6502 assembly language for fun, its a lot faster and easier than the first time on actual hardware when I was a teenager.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Been using a book I picked up from eBay &lt;a href="https://www.goodreads.com/book/show/2911575-discovering-bbc-micro-machine"&gt;Discovering BBC Micro Machine Code by A.P. Stephenson&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Using &lt;a href="https://github.com/stardot/beebasm/"&gt;BeebAsm assembler&lt;/a&gt; on my Mac with a BBC Micro emulator, rather than build in BBC BASIC one.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;You can find my code at Github &lt;a href="https://github.com/alastairhm/beebasm"&gt;https://github.com/alastairhm/beebasm&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This example draws a line of zeros to Mode 7, see screenshot below.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>10 PRINT</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10print/</link><pubDate>Fri, 04 Sep 2020 16:08:20 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/10print/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;BBC Micro take on &lt;a href="https://10print.org/"&gt;C64 10 Print&lt;/a&gt; one line random pattern generator.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="code-block"&gt;&#10; &lt;button class="code-copy" type="button" hidden aria-label="Copy code to clipboard"&gt;&#10; &lt;span class="code-copy-label" aria-hidden="true"&gt;Copy&lt;/span&gt;&#10; &lt;/button&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" style="color:#f8f8f2;background-color:#272822;-moz-tab-size:4;-o-tab-size:4;tab-size:4;-webkit-text-size-adjust:none;"&gt;&lt;code class="language-text" data-lang="text"&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;10 MODE 0&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;20 N=RND(1):IF N &amp;gt; 0.5 THEN PRINT &amp;#34;/&amp;#34;; ELSE PRINT &amp;#34;\&amp;#34;;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;30 GOTO 20&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="display:flex;"&gt;&lt;span&gt;RUN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://t.co/xQag2GKwx0"&gt;Twitter Post&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Golden Tail and Kitsune's Curse New Retro Game</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/goldentail/</link><pubDate>Wed, 26 Aug 2020 09:08:22 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/goldentail/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;New retro game, looks worth getting a Amstrad CPC emulator setup to play it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe id="lbry-iframe" width="560" height="315" src="https://lbry.tv/$/embed/amstrad-cpc-golden-tail-and-kitsune-s/95790dfec48b00467037e730b8c610716e5ccf52" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://lbry.tv/@retrorecollections:a"&gt;Video Source Retro Collection&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Juan&amp;rsquo;s games: (&lt;a href="https://www.usebox.net/jjm/"&gt;https://www.usebox.net/jjm/&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Buy physical copies of these games:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.polyplay.xyz/navi.php?qs=golden+tail"&gt;Golden Tail&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://www.polyplay.xyz/navi.php?qs=Kitsune+curse"&gt;Kitsune Curse&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Mree</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/mree/</link><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2020 13:51:27 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/mree/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Mr. Ee from Micro Power for the BBC Micro nice variation on the Pacman theme.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe id="lbry-iframe" width="560" height="315" src="https://lbry.tv/$/embed/BBC-Mirco-MrEE/8c37287bd9782db6434ff90701d3909bb9843b5c" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://www.bbcmicro.co.uk/game.php?id=85"&gt;Play Online at BBC Mirco&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Acorn Electron Sound Mod</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/acornmod/</link><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2020 08:31:48 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/acornmod/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Interest video about modding the Acorn Electron.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe id="lbry-iframe" width="560" height="315" src="https://lbry.tv/$/embed/acorn-electron-audio-out-scart-mod/60586299238a4928e8493fe5532f2ff890b7dbee" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>The Pit New Retro Game</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/thepit/</link><pubDate>Thu, 13 Aug 2020 09:08:22 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/thepit/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;New retro game, looks worth getting a Commodore emulator setup to play it.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This style of game is one of my favorites, loved Boulder Dash and Repton.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe id="lbry-iframe" width="560" height="315" src="https://lbry.tv/$/embed/8bit-nibble-the-pit-new-commodore-plus-4/2059e72eb0251e8a354e20834b0c9ee58f0e46e9" allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://lbry.tv/@retrorecollections:a"&gt;Video Source Retro Collection&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20260305064809/http://plus4world.powweb.com/software/The_Pit"&gt;The Pit Download&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20210422064903/http://plus4world.powweb.com/play/the_pit"&gt;Play Online&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Retro Gaming Commando</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/commando/</link><pubDate>Wed, 12 Aug 2020 08:57:44 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/commando/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;One of the games I loved playing in my youth on my BBC Micro, I&amp;rsquo;m still rubbish at it to this day.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div style="position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden;"&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&#9;&lt;iframe allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share; fullscreen" loading="eager" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/zbXRDb63hH0?autoplay=0&amp;amp;controls=1&amp;amp;end=0&amp;amp;loop=0&amp;amp;mute=0&amp;amp;start=0" style="position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; border:0;" title="YouTube video"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;&#10;&#9;&#9;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&#10;&lt;h2 id="links"&gt;Links&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://bbcmicro.co.uk/game.php?id=2412"&gt;Play Online at BBC Mirco&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://gamefaqs.gamespot.com/bbc/946950-commando"&gt;Game FAQs&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Cubes #retro</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/cubes-retro/</link><pubDate>Thu, 04 Jan 2018 15:05:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/cubes-retro/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src='https://farm5.staticflickr.com/4683/38788227884_05f29cf3f5_b.jpg' style='max-width:586px;' /&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div&gt;via Instagram &lt;a href="http://bit.ly/2E4BXbz" rel="nofollow"&gt;bit.ly/2E4BXbz&lt;/a&gt; January 04, 2018 at 01:44PM http://bit.ly/2lSucyd, January 04, 2018 at 01:44PM&lt;/div&gt;</description></item><item><title>Make a Raspberry Pi Portable Arcade Console (with Retropie)</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/make-raspberry-pi-portable-arcade/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Aug 2016 09:10:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/make-raspberry-pi-portable-arcade/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Looks like a cool project without doing a full arcade machine.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;iframe allowfullscreen="" frameborder="0" height="270" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/bYHXUECdQAg" width="480"&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;</description></item><item><title>Killer Gorilla on the BBC Micro</title><link>https://blog.0x32.co.uk/posts/killer-gorilla-on-bbc-micro/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 Jul 2016 12:18:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>h